 Nation","person_id":"tvfy_11060","person_slug":"tyron-whitten","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Varun Ghosh","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_11017","person_slug":"varun-ghosh","vote":"no"}],"name":"Matters of Urgency — Veterans","noes":21,"question":"Glenn Sterle Senator Cash has submitted a proposal, under standing order 75, today, which has been circulated and is shown on the Dynamic Red: That, in the opinion of the Senate, the following is a matter of urgency: The serious failure of judgement demonstrated by the Minister for Veterans' Affairs in initially declining to meet veterans and bereaved family members who came to Parliament House to raise urgent concerns about their health care, and the question of whether the minister retains the confidence of the veteran community he is entrusted to serve. Is consideration of the proposal supported? _More than the number of senators required by the standing orders having risen in their places—_ With the concurrence of the Senate, the clerks will set the clock in line with the informal arrangements made by the whips. Michaelia Cash I move: That, in the opinion of the Senate, the following is a matter of urgency: The serious failure of judgement demonstrated by the Minister for Veterans' Affairs in initially declining to meet veterans and bereaved family members who came to Parliament House to raise urgent concerns about their health care, and the question of whether the minister retains the confidence of the veteran community he is entrusted to serve. Minister Keogh has sadly lost the confidence of the veterans he is supposed to support and champion on a daily basis. In their own words—this is an indictment on any minister—he has lost their trust. He has lost their respect. On that basis alone, it is no longer tenable that Minister Keogh hold the position of Minister for Veterans' Affairs and Minister for Defence Personnel. Our veterans are the Australians who put on the uniform, and they put it on proudly. They are the people who serve this country. They are the people who are prepared to put themselves in harm's way so that they can defend the freedoms that each and every one of us has on a daily basis. They should never have to fight their own government and, in p","result":"affirmative","slug":"division-federal-senate-10699","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2026-08-19/4"}
